# The Python dependencies of the trainer's CPU tests (#1044, #1171), the INPUT of requirements-ci.txt.
# .github/workflows/trainer.yml installs the compiled file, which pins every package by content (`pip install --require-hashes`),
# and runs experiments/toolchat/native/run_tests.py. Only what the suite imports: the trainer's tiny CPU model (torch, transformers),
# the checkpoint soup (safetensors) and numpy. The VM's trainer needs more (flash-linear-attention, CUDA); none of it is exercised on
# a CPU. peft and zstandard are below: the tests run a LoRA step and read .zst.
#
# Regenerate after changing this file, from experiments/toolchat/native (uv; every package and file it lists is then
# re-hashed, so review the diff of the .txt):
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-ci.in --generate-hashes --emit-index-url --python-version 3.11 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
#     --index-strategy unsafe-first-match --exclude-newer <two weeks ago> -o requirements-ci.txt
#
# PyPI is the higher-priority extra index: the CPU index mirrors some unrelated wheels without upload dates.
# The exact +cpu torch pin falls back to the CPU index; every other existing pin keeps its PyPI provenance.
# The current security refresh used global cutoff 2026-10-19T23:59:59Z and the narrow override
# --exclude-newer-package certifi=2026-10-20T02:25:00Z for GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2. Certifi 2026.10.19
# restores the unaffected roots removed in 2026.10.18. filelock 4.2.1 and setuptools 84.1.0 fit the global cutoff.
# The exact regeneration command is recorded in requirements-ci.txt; unrelated pins stay unchanged.
#
# Check the result before committing: `osv-scanner scan source -L requirements-ci.txt` reports no advisory today.

# CPU wheel (download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu): PyPI's Linux wheel is the CUDA build, a gigabyte with the nvidia-* libraries.
# 2.13.0, not the 2.8.0 train/vm/run_job.sh installs on the VM: OSV lists eight advisories on 2.8.0, four of them rated high
# (among them CVE-2026-24747, memory corruption in the weights_only unpickler, fixed in 2.10.0), and none on 2.13.0. These
# tests build a tiny random model and never load a checkpoint of the VM's, so the version carries no result across.
torch==2.13.0+cpu

# The version train/bundle.py stages for a job (`--transformers`) and train/kaggle/kernel.py installs, which is the one the tiny-model tests build against.
transformers==5.17.0

numpy
safetensors

# M6 (#1171): the arm-C LoRA test (peft) and the datagen reader (zstandard).
peft
zstandard
